# Always link the paper draft

Whenever you discuss the paper, figures, captions, layout, regenerating plots for the manuscript, or anything in `paper/`:

1. **Link the draft with an absolute `file:///` URL** that resolves on this machine, e.g.
   `[paper/draft.md](file:///C:/Users/toviah.moldwin/Code/statistical_learning-1/paper/draft.md)`.
2. Before sending the link, **verify the file exists** (`Test-Path` / `Resolve-Path`). Do not use a relative `](paper/draft.md)` chat link alone — those break in chat.
3. If you changed figures or collect into `paper/figures/`, include the same verified link so the user can reopen/refresh the preview.

Do this even for short status replies about paper work.
